{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": [
    "Explicit segment -> archetype pins, and the archetypes' pinned peer sets.",
    "",
    "Keyword containment alone classified 11 of 58 segments (19%) and got three",
    "of those eleven WRONG: AMD's Gaming segment is console and GPU silicon, not",
    "a games publisher, but 'gaming' matched games_media and would have valued",
    "it against EA and Take-Two. A miss falls through to the LLM and shows up as",
    "variance; a false positive produces a confident wrong number. So an",
    "explicit (ticker, segment) pin always wins over keyword inference.",
    "",
    "PEER SETS ARE INVESTMENT JUDGEMENT, NOT DATA. They are the load-bearing",
    "assumption in the whole SOTP and belong under review and version control,",
    "not regenerated per run. Bump `version` when a peer set changes so a",
    "valuation can be traced to the peer set that produced it.",
    "",
    "archetype null = this split is not a valuation split. Costco's segments are",
    "merchandise categories sharing one warehouse P&L; Cisco's overlap three",
    "different cuts of the same revenue; 'All Other' is a residual. Valuing",
    "these as businesses invents precision, so they fall back to the group."
  ],

